{"id":9790,"artist":"Traditional","title":"House of the Rising Sun","lyrics_plain":"There is a house in New Orleans,\nthey call the Rising Sun.\nAnd it's been the ruin of many a poor boy,\nand God, I know I'm one.\nMy mother was a tailor,\nsewed my new blue jeans.\nMy father was a gamblin' man,\non down in New Orleans.\nThe only thing a gambler needs,\nis a suitcase and trunk.\nAnd the only time, he'll be satisfied,\nis when he's all a drunk.\nOh! mother, tell your children,\nNot to do what I have done.\nSpend your lives in sin and misery,\nIn the House of the Rising Sun.\nGot one foot on the platform.\nThe other foot on the train.\nI'm going back to New Orleans,\nto wear that ball and chain.\nWell, there is a house in New Orleans,\nThey call the Rising Sun,\nAnd it's been the ruin of many a poor boy,\nand God, I know I'm one.","lyrics_synced":"[00:16.97] There is a house in New Orleans,\n[00:23.49] they call the Rising Sun.\n[00:29.90] And it's been the ruin of many a poor boy,\n[00:36.55] and God, I know I'm one.\n[00:52.96] My mother was a tailor,\n[00:59.78] sewed my new blue jeans.\n[01:06.03] My father was a gamblin' man,\n[01:12.56] on down in New Orleans.\n[01:28.96] The only thing a gambler needs,\n[01:35.50] is a suitcase and trunk.\n[01:42.03] And the only time, he'll be satisfied,\n[01:48.56] is when he's all a drunk.\n[02:39.09] Oh! mother, tell your children,\n[02:45.37] Not to do what I have done.\n[02:52.46] Spend your lives in sin and misery,\n[02:58.71] In the House of the Rising Sun.\n[03:14.84] Got one foot on the platform.\n[03:21.09] The other foot on the train.\n[03:27.34] I'm going back to New Orleans,\n[03:33.59] to wear that ball and chain.\n[03:47.98] Well, there is a house in New Orleans,\n[03:55.50] They call the Rising Sun,\n[04:01.68] And it's been the ruin of many a poor boy,\n[04:08.04] and God, I know I'm one.","lyrics_synced_enhanced":"[00:16.00] <00:16.00>There <00:16.25>is\n[00:17.75] <00:17.75>a <00:18.00>house\n[00:19.50] <00:1